      options: ["Because e = 1 − Tc/Th is the formula for an ideal (Carnot) engine only — a real engine's actual efficiency (here 30%) is always lower", "Because real engines never lose any heat", "Because the formula only applies to refrigerators", "Because Tc and Th must be in Celsius for real engines"], answer: "Because e = 1 − Tc/Th is the formula for an ideal (Carnot) engine only — a real engine's actual efficiency (here 30%) is always lower",
